{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789332614,"nonce":"aRwm6tHe43sU1pSQ6mFwdpsw/vU=","title":"A trap armed in the caller's own storage","message":"Arming a trap took a pooled context and zeroed all of it, jmp_buf\nincluded, though setjmp writes the buffer in full; a host that traps\naround every call into compiled code paid that plus the pool's push and\npop each time. `hlp_setup_trap_in(storage, size)` arms the trap in\nstorage the caller keeps, its own C frame, writing the few fields a trap\nneeds; a context so armed is never retired into the pool. The pooled\npath arms a reused context the same way instead of rebuilding it.","files":null}]}